IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cbr-nouns`
IMPORT `cbr-reg2-benefits`

-- TESTS OF REGULATION 2(6) (the specified benefits) AND REGULATION 2(5) (src:35-50).
-- Expected values are written from the text; the reason is given beside each group.

§ `Tests of regulation 2(5) and (6)`

-- A payment, built from its six facts, in the order of the record.
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of payment made for the week`
      entitles IS A BOOLEAN
      instrument IS AN `Instrument granting an allowance for a child on a death due to service or war injury`
      accepted IS A BOOLEAN
      paid IS A BOOLEAN
      forchild IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Payment made for the week`
`a payment of kind` kind entitles instrument accepted paid forchild MEANS
    `Payment made for the week` WITH
        `kind of payment` IS kind
        `receipt of the benefit entitles the recipient to an increase for dependants specified in the Table in Schedule 4 to that Act` IS entitles
        `instrument granting the allowance` IS instrument
        `the Commissioners accept the allowance as analogous to one granted under those instruments` IS accepted
        `paid to the claimant in respect of the week` IS paid
        `paid in respect of the child or qualifying young person` IS forchild

-- A child, built from the one fact paragraph (5)(b) reads.
GIVEN eldest IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Child or qualifying young person at the start of the week`
`a child who is the only or eldest, or not` eldest MEANS
    `Child or qualifying young person at the start of the week` WITH
        `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 2010
        `child benefit is payable to the claimant in respect of the child or qualifying young person` IS TRUE
        `a child for the purposes of child benefit` IS TRUE
        `where the young person is` IS `in Great Britain`
        `a qualifying young person for the purposes of Part 9 of SSCBA` IS FALSE
        `a qualifying young person for the purposes of Part 9 of SSCB(NI)A` IS FALSE
        `the only person, or the elder or eldest person, in respect of whom child benefit is payable to the claimant` IS eldest
        `the claimant resides with a parent of the child or qualifying young person` IS FALSE
        `the claimant resides with that parent as mentioned in paragraph (2)(a)` IS FALSE

`none listed` MEANS `an instrument not listed in paragraph (6)(c)(i) to (vii)`
`the death-in-service allowance` MEANS `an allowance for a child or a qualifying young person granted in respect of the death of a person due to service or war injury`

§§ `Regulation 2(6)(a) (src:39-40): a benefit under SSCBA whose receipt entitles to a Schedule 4 increase`

#ASSERT `a payment is a specified benefit under paragraph (6)(a)` (`a payment of kind` `a benefit under SSCBA` TRUE `none listed` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- Under SSCBA but receipt does not entitle to the increase: not (a).
#ASSERT NOT (`a payment is a specified benefit under paragraph (6)(a)` (`a payment of kind` `a benefit under SSCBA` FALSE `none listed` FALSE TRUE TRUE))
-- The increase is there but the benefit is under the Northern Ireland Act: not (a), it is (b).
#ASSERT NOT (`a payment is a specified benefit under paragraph (6)(a)` (`a payment of kind` `a benefit under SSCB(NI)A` TRUE `none listed` FALSE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT `a payment is a specified benefit` (`a payment of kind` `a benefit under SSCBA` TRUE `none listed` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a payment is a specified benefit` (`a payment of kind` `a benefit under SSCBA` FALSE `none listed` FALSE TRUE TRUE))

§§ `Regulation 2(6)(b) (src:41): a benefit under SSCB(NI)A whose receipt entitles to a Schedule 4 increase`

#ASSERT `a payment is a specified benefit under paragraph (6)(b)` (`a payment of kind` `a benefit under SSCB(NI)A` TRUE `none listed` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a payment is a specified benefit under paragraph (6)(b)` (`a payment of kind` `a benefit under SSCB(NI)A` FALSE `none listed` FALSE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`a payment is a specified benefit under paragraph (6)(b)` (`a payment of kind` `a benefit under SSCBA` TRUE `none listed` FALSE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT `a payment is a specified benefit` (`a payment of kind` `a benefit under SSCB(NI)A` TRUE `none listed` FALSE TRUE TRUE)

§§ `Regulation 2(6)(c)(i) to (vii) (src:42-49): an allowance for a child on a death due to service or war injury, under a listed instrument`

#ASSERT `a payment is a specified benefit under paragraph (6)(c)(i) to (vii)` (`a payment of kind` `the death-in-service allowance` FALSE `the Armed Forces and Reserve Forces (Compensation Scheme) Order 2005` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `a payment is a specified benefit under paragraph (6)(c)(i) to (vii)` (`a payment of kind` `the death-in-service allowance` FALSE `the Naval, Military and Air Forces Etc. (Disablement and Death) Service Pensions Order 1983` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `a payment is a specified benefit under paragraph (6)(c)(i) to (vii)` (`a payment of kind` `the death-in-service allowance` FALSE `the Pensions (Polish Forces) Scheme 1964` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `a payment is a specified benefit under paragraph (6)(c)(i) to (vii)` (`a payment of kind` `the death-in-service allowance` FALSE `the War Pensions (Mercantile Marine) Scheme 1964` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `a payment is a specified benefit under paragraph (6)(c)(i) to (vii)` (`a payment of kind` `the death-in-service allowance` FALSE `the Warrant of 21st December 1964 concerning pensions and grants in respect of disablement or death due to service in the Home Guard` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `a payment is a specified benefit under paragraph (6)(c)(i) to (vii)` (`a payment of kind` `the death-in-service allowance` FALSE `the Order of 22nd December 1964 concerning pensions and grants in respect of disablement or death due to service in the Home Guard after 27th April 1952` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `a payment is a specified benefit under paragraph (6)(c)(i) to (vii)` (`a payment of kind` `the death-in-service allowance` FALSE `the Order by Her Majesty dated 4th January 1971 in respect of service in the Ulster Defence Regiment` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- An instrument not on the list, and no acceptance by the Commissioners: not (i) to (vii).
#ASSERT NOT (`a payment is a specified benefit under paragraph (6)(c)(i) to (vii)` (`a payment of kind` `the death-in-service allowance` FALSE `none listed` FALSE TRUE TRUE))
-- A listed instrument, but not an allowance for a child on a death in service (a payment of another kind).
#ASSERT NOT (`a payment is a specified benefit under paragraph (6)(c)(i) to (vii)` (`a payment of kind` `a payment of some other kind` FALSE `the Pensions (Polish Forces) Scheme 1964` FALSE TRUE TRUE))

§§ `Regulation 2(6)(c)(viii) (src:50): an allowance the Commissioners accept as analogous`

-- The judgment is the Commissioners', taken as an input: accepted.
#ASSERT `a payment is a specified benefit under paragraph (6)(c)(viii)` (`a payment of kind` `the death-in-service allowance` FALSE `none listed` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `a payment is a specified benefit` (`a payment of kind` `the death-in-service allowance` FALSE `none listed` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- Not accepted: neither (i) to (vii) nor (viii).
#ASSERT NOT (`a payment is a specified benefit under paragraph (6)(c)(viii)` (`a payment of kind` `the death-in-service allowance` FALSE `none listed` FALSE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`a payment is a specified benefit` (`a payment of kind` `the death-in-service allowance` FALSE `none listed` FALSE TRUE TRUE))
-- Accepted, but the payment is not an allowance for a child on a death in service: (viii) is about such allowances only.
#ASSERT NOT (`a payment is a specified benefit under paragraph (6)(c)(viii)` (`a payment of kind` `a payment of some other kind` FALSE `none listed` TRUE TRUE TRUE))

§§ `A payment of some other kind is never a specified benefit`

#ASSERT NOT (`a payment is a specified benefit` (`a payment of kind` `a payment of some other kind` TRUE `the Pensions (Polish Forces) Scheme 1964` TRUE TRUE TRUE))

§§ `Regulation 2(5) (src:35-38): a specified benefit paid to the person for the only, elder or eldest child gives the enhanced rate`

-- All of (a), (b) and the specified benefit.
#ASSERT `paragraph (5) gives the enhanced rate for the child` (`a payment of kind` `a benefit under SSCBA` TRUE `none listed` FALSE TRUE TRUE) (`a child who is the only or eldest, or not` TRUE)
-- Limb (a) fails: the payment is not paid to the person.
#ASSERT NOT (`paragraph (5) gives the enhanced rate for the child` (`a payment of kind` `a benefit under SSCBA` TRUE `none listed` FALSE FALSE TRUE) (`a child who is the only or eldest, or not` TRUE))
-- Limb (b) fails, in the payment: it is not paid in respect of the child.
#ASSERT NOT (`paragraph (5) gives the enhanced rate for the child` (`a payment of kind` `a benefit under SSCBA` TRUE `none listed` FALSE TRUE FALSE) (`a child who is the only or eldest, or not` TRUE))
-- Limb (b) fails, in the child: not the only, elder or eldest child.
#ASSERT NOT (`paragraph (5) gives the enhanced rate for the child` (`a payment of kind` `a benefit under SSCBA` TRUE `none listed` FALSE TRUE TRUE) (`a child who is the only or eldest, or not` FALSE))
-- The payment is not a specified benefit.
#ASSERT NOT (`paragraph (5) gives the enhanced rate for the child` (`a payment of kind` `a benefit under SSCBA` FALSE `none listed` FALSE TRUE TRUE) (`a child who is the only or eldest, or not` TRUE))
-- Each of the other kinds of specified benefit works the same way.
#ASSERT `paragraph (5) gives the enhanced rate for the child` (`a payment of kind` `a benefit under SSCB(NI)A` TRUE `none listed` FALSE TRUE TRUE) (`a child who is the only or eldest, or not` TRUE)
#ASSERT `paragraph (5) gives the enhanced rate for the child` (`a payment of kind` `the death-in-service allowance` FALSE `the Pensions (Polish Forces) Scheme 1964` FALSE TRUE TRUE) (`a child who is the only or eldest, or not` TRUE)
#ASSERT `paragraph (5) gives the enhanced rate for the child` (`a payment of kind` `the death-in-service allowance` FALSE `none listed` TRUE TRUE TRUE) (`a child who is the only or eldest, or not` TRUE)
